.TH VECTOR 3 "2026" "y-- standard library" "y-- Library Reference"
.SH NAME
Vector \- mathematical vector type and constructor
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B Vector
module enables the
.B vector()
value type and exposes a global
.B vector
constructor function.
Importing this module sets a flag in the interpreter that allows vector
literals and vector operator overloading.
.PP
For methods on vector values (dot, cross, magnitude, unitVec, projectOnto,
dimension, vector_reversal, expand, shrink), see
.BR vector (3)
in the ValueTypeDoc reference.
.SH FUNCTIONS
.SS vector
.TP
\fBSYNOPSIS\fR
vector() vector(x: float(), y: float(), z: float(), ...)
.TP
\fBDESCRIPTION\fR
Creates an n-dimensional vector from its numeric arguments.
If called with no arguments, returns a 3D zero vector <0.0, 0.0, 0.0>.
Each argument must be a numeric value; non-numeric arguments raise
.BR TypeError .
.TP
\fBRETURN VALUE\fR
vector()
.TP
\fBERRORS\fR
\fBTypeError\fR \- if any argument is non-numeric.
.TP
\fBEXAMPLES\fR
.EX
vector()            -> <0.0, 0.0, 0.0>
vector(1.0, 2.0)    -> <1.0, 2.0>
.EE
.SH "SEE ALSO"
vector(3), Math(3)
